%% args
list
-h

%% stdout
usage: envctl list [file]
alias: envctl ls

Prints the active key names one per line in file order. --values appends each
value under the redaction rules, and --all adds the commented keys tagged
(disabled). A masked multiline value collapses to one line; an unmasked one
shows its first line.

Flags:
  --values              also print values
  --all                 also print disabled keys
  --sort                print entries sorted by key
  --env                 use the process environment instead of a file
  --redact              mask secret-looking values
  --raw                 shorthand for --redact=never --show-control-chars
  --show-control-chars  print control bytes as they are
  --paranoid            apply the entropy bar to every value

Full reference: man envctl
